# Data validation

ALWAYS validate Supabase query results with Zod before use.

- Schemas live in `lib/schemas/database.ts` (match the selected columns)
- Use `safeParse()`, never bare `parse()`
- On failure: `console.error` with `[functionName]`, `z.prettifyError`, and raw JSON; return a safe default or fail the action

```typescript
const parsed = Schema.safeParse(data);
if (!parsed.success) {
  console.error("[functionName] Zod validation failed:", z.prettifyError(parsed.error));
  console.error("[functionName] Raw data:", JSON.stringify(data, null, 2));
  return defaultValue;
}
return parsed.data;
```
